From 6220524bf62b427f94f5016871badb6ef932bbf9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:08:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban CI wait: read a PR ref, so a conflicting PR
 (no pull_request run can start) wakes its owner

Why: 2026-11-13, card t_01a1d5dae3fe181b parked (awaiting kind=ci) on
"https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/2495 checks @7072089bad...". The PR conflicted with
`state`, so GitHub started no pull_request workflow for that head (0 runs; REST mergeable still null 9 min after
the push). kanban_ci_progress only read refs naming <repo>/actions/runs/<id>; a PR ref was `untracked`, so neither
confirm() at park time nor sweep() while parked noticed, and the owner would have slept to its 1 h cap on a
producer that could not fire. Kanban card t_01a1d645e8f07158.

What:
- pr_target(ref, hint): <slug>/pull/<n> plus an optional head sha (@<7-40 hex>, or a 40-hex sha in the ref or
  the park's wake check/reason). A ref naming a run keeps the run path.
- pr_progress(repo, n, sha, parked_at): closed/merged or head moved off the sha -> ok (the card's own probe
  answers); mergeable false / mergeable_state dirty -> not_starting ("PR #N conflicts with <base>: pull_request
  checks cannot start until it is rebased"); no workflow run for the head QUEUED_LIMIT_SECONDS after the later of
  the park and the PR's updated_at -> not_starting ("no CI run was created for <sha> in 15 min (PR #N
  mergeable=<v>)"); queued runs of the head go through ci_run_progress (runner offline/busy detection);
  mergeable null with runs -> unknown (settling, no warning).
- confirm() refuses a park on a conflicting PR (ci_run_unstartable, naming the PR, base and rebase); 0 runs at
  park time is allowed (a fresh push has none yet).
- sweep() includes PR-ref waits under the same RECHECK_SECONDS / per-sweep budget. A per-PR not_starting wakes the
  card with one kanban-dispatcher comment and no runners-offline shared blocker (one PR's cause, not a pool's).
- GitHub errors fail open with the existing warnings.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_ci_progress_pr.py (acceptance a-g, 19 tests) RED on origin/main (18 fail,
the park-allowed control passes), GREEN here; every test file importing kanban_ci_progress or kanban_awaiting
(21 files, 783 tests) passes; scripts/check --base origin/main ok.
